{
  "description": "issue #792: `tell [ :a :b ]` then `hide_turtle` and `show_turtle` each apply once per addressed turtle, emitting one `visibility-change` per turtle carrying its own `turtle_id` (1 then 2). `hide_turtle` fans out first (true->false for turtles 1 and 2) so that `show_turtle` has an observable effect — `show_turtle` on an already-visible turtle is a no-op that emits nothing (spec/rendering.md's avatar-visibility idempotence), so this fixture first hides both turtles, then `show_turtle` fans out (false->true for turtles 1 and 2). The events are stamped because the addressed set is now explicit (a `tell` has run). Every change of the addressed set — here from `tell` — also emits the addressing `primitive` event carrying `addressing: { addressed_turtle_ids, current_turtle_id }` (issue #766, spec/rendering.md:193). Closes the `show_turtle` execution-coverage gap the Sprites Epic Gate recorded (issue #792): `show_turtle` previously appeared only in a `check: true` fixture (`shape-checks-clean`) and was never executed under Sprites addressing.",
